hadiths[67]{hadithnumber,text}:
"425","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would begin the prayer, he would raise both his hands up to the level of his shoulders, and when he said the takbeer for bowing (ruku‘), and when he raised his head from ruku‘, he would also raise both hands in the same way and say: “Sami‘ Allahu liman hamidah, Rabbana wa lakal hamd.” But he would not do this (raising of hands) in the two prostrations (sujood). Nafi‘ narrates that when Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) would enter the prayer, he would first say the opening takbeer (takbeer tahrimah) and simultaneously raise his hands. Similarly, when he would bow (ruku‘), and when he would say “Sami‘ Allahu liman hamidah,” he would also raise both hands, and when he would rise from the first sitting (qa‘dah oola), he would also raise his hands. He attributed this action to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), (that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray in this manner)."
"426","Sahih Sahl bin Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) says that people were instructed (by the Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him) to place the right hand on the left wrist during prayer."
"427","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, Abu Bakr Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, and Umar Farooq, may Allah be pleased with him, used to begin the prayer with (Alhamdulillahi Rabbil 'Alamin)."
"428","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to observe a pause between the Takbir and the recitation (of the Qur'an). I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! May my parents be sacrificed for you, what do you recite during the pause between the Takbir and the recitation?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I say (this supplication): O Allah! Set a distance between me and my sins as You have set a distance between the East and the West. O Allah! Purify me from sins as a white garment is cleansed from dirt. O Allah! Wash away my sins with water, snow, and hail."""
"429","Narrated from Sayyida Asma bint Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with her), the hadith regarding the prayer of eclipse has already been mentioned. (See Hadith: Book: Statement of Knowledge... Chapter: The person who answered a fatwa by gesture of hand or head...). In this narration, she says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""At that time, Paradise came so close to me that if I had dared, I would have brought one of its bunches to you, and Hell also came close to me until I said, 'O my Lord! Will I be included among these people?' Suddenly, my gaze fell upon a woman."" I think the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A cat was scratching her. I asked, 'What happened to her?' The people said that she had tied up the cat until it died of hunger. This (woman) neither fed it nor let it go so that it could eat the insects of the earth (like mice, etc.)."" (Nafi' was doubtful whether it was 'khushaysh' or 'khushash al-ard' that was said.)"
"430","“In the original manuscript, Hadiths ‘429 and 430’ have been combined. (Ibn Ibrahim)”"
"431","It was asked from Sayyiduna Khabbab (may Allah be pleased with him) whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite (something) in the Zuhr and Asr prayers? Khabbab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Yes. It was asked: By what did you distinguish this? So Khabbab (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: By the movement of the blessed beard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"432","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is wrong with people that they raise their gaze towards the sky during their prayer?"" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) spoke very sternly about this until he said: ""They must stop doing this, or their eyesight will be taken away."""
"433","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about looking here and there during prayer. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is a snatching of Satan; he snatches from a person's prayer."""
"434","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the people of Kufa complained to the Commander of the Faithful, Umar Farooq, about Sayyiduna Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him), so the Commander of the Faithful removed Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) and appointed Sayyiduna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him) as their governor. The people made many complaints (against Sayyiduna Sa’d), to the extent that they said he does not lead the prayer well. So the Commander of the Faithful (may Allah be pleased with him) summoned him and said, “O Abu Ishaq!” (this is the kunyah of Sa’d, may Allah be pleased with him), “these people say that you do not lead the prayer well.” He replied, “Listen! By Allah, I lead them in prayer just as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to lead us. I would prolong the first two rak’ahs and shorten the last two.” Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “O Abu Ishaq! This is what I thought of you.” Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) sent a man or a delegation with Sayyiduna Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) to Kufa so that they could ask the people of Kufa about Sayyiduna Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him). (So they went) and did not leave any mosque without asking about Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him), and all the people praised him highly, until they came to the mosque of Banu Abs. There, a man stood up—his name was Usamah bin Qatadah and his kunyah was Abu Sa’dah. He said, “Since you have made us swear (to tell the truth), (I am compelled to say) that Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) would not go out with the army (for jihad himself), nor would he distribute (the spoils) equally, nor was he just in his judgments.” Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him), upon hearing this, said, “Look, I make three supplications against you: O Allah! If this servant is lying and has stood up for show and fame, then lengthen his life, increase his poverty, and subject him to trials.” (And so it happened.) Afterwards, when he was asked about his condition, he would say, “I am an old man, afflicted by trials; I have been struck by the supplication of Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him).” Abdul Malik (the narrator of the hadith) says, “I saw him in this state: his eyebrows had drooped over his eyes due to old age, he would harass girls in the streets and molest them.”"
"435","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The prayer of the one who does not recite Surah Al-Fatihah is not valid."""
"436","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once entered the mosque. At that time, a man came and offered prayer, then he greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned the greeting and said: ""Go back and pray, for you have not prayed."" So he went back and prayed as he had prayed before, then returned and greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Go back and pray, for you have not prayed."" (This happened) three times. Then he said, ""By Him Who has sent you with the truth, I cannot pray better than this, so please teach me."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you stand for prayer, say the takbeer, then recite whatever you know from the Qur'an, then bow until you are at ease in bowing, then rise until you are standing straight, then prostrate until you are at ease in prostration, then raise your head until you are sitting at ease, and do this throughout your prayer."""
"437","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Surah Al-Fatihah and (some) other two surahs in the first two rak‘ahs of the Zuhr prayer. In the first rak‘ah, he would recite at length, and in the second, he would recite a shorter surah than the first. Sometimes he would make us hear a verse. In the ‘Asr prayer, he would recite Surah Al-Fatihah and two other surahs, reciting a long surah in the first rak‘ah and a shorter one in the second. In the first rak‘ah of the Fajr prayer, he would also recite a long surah, and in the second rak‘ah, a shorter surah than the first."
"438","Narrated Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): (My mother) Umm Fadl (may Allah be pleased with her) once heard me reciting (Al-Mursalat 'Urfa) in prayer. She said, ""O my son! By reciting this Surah, you have reminded me that this is the last Surah I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). He used to recite it in the Maghrib prayer."""
"439","Sayyiduna Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) reciting one of the two long surahs in the Maghrib prayer."
"440","Jubair bin Mut'im (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting Surah At-Tur in the Maghrib prayer."
"441","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): I prayed behind Abul-Qasim (ﷺ), and he recited ( ""When the sky has split open"" ) and performed a prostration (at this place in the Surah), so I will continue to perform prostration in it until I meet him."
"442","Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and he recited (Wat-Teen waz-Zaytoon) in the ‘Isha (night) prayer. And in another narration, he says: I have not heard anyone with a more pleasant voice or better recitation than him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"443","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says that in all prayers the Qur'an is recited. Then, in those (prayers) in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited aloud to us, we (also) recite aloud to you, and in those (prayers) in which he recited quietly and concealed from us, we (also) conceal from you. And if you do not recite more than Surah Al-Fatihah, it is sufficient, and if you recite more, it is better."
"444","´Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrates that (one day) the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out with some of his companions intending to go towards the market of ‘Ukaz. (At that time) a barrier had been placed between the devils and the news of the heavens, and flaming fire was being thrown at them. So the devils returned to their people. Their people said, “What has happened to you? (This time you have not brought anything.)” The devils replied, “A barrier has been set up between us and the news of the heavens, and now flaming fire is being hurled at us.” Their people said, “Something has created a barrier between you and the news of the heavens which has just appeared, so travel throughout the earth, east and west, and see what is that thing which has created a barrier between you and the news of the heavens.” So they set out in search, and those who came towards Tihamah reached the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who was at that time at the place of Nakhlah, intending to go to the market of ‘Ukaz, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was performing the Fajr prayer with his companions. When those jinn heard the Qur’an, they kept listening to it. They said, “By Allah! This is what has created a barrier between you and the news of the heavens.” So when they returned to their people from there, they said, “O our people! We have heard a wondrous Qur’an which guides to the right path, so we have believed in it, and (now) we will never associate anyone with our Lord.” (Surah Al-Jinn: 72) So Allah Almighty revealed these verses (of Surah Al-Jinn) to His beloved Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ((Say: It has been revealed to me)) (Surah Al-Jinn: 1), and the conversation of the jinn was conveyed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"445","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited aloud in those prayers in which he was commanded to do so, and remained silent in those in which he was commanded to do so. And ""Your Lord is not forgetful"" (that He would give a wrong command by mistake. Surah Maryam: 64). ""Indeed, for you in the Messenger of Allah (the actions and sayings) is a good example."" (Surah Al-Ahzab: 21)."
"446","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came to him and said: ""I recited a Mufassal surah in one rak'ah at night,"" and he said, ""I recited it as quickly as poetry is recited."" Indeed, I know those similar surahs which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite together, then he mentioned twenty Mufassal surahs (that from these) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite two surahs in each rak'ah."
"447","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Surah Al-Fatihah and two other surahs in the first two rak'ahs of Zuhr, and in the last two rak'ahs (only) Umm al-Kitab (i.e., Surah Al-Fatihah). And sometimes he would make us hear a verse, and he would prolong the first rak'ah more than the second, and the same was the case in Asr and likewise in Fajr."
"448","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the Imam says Ameen, you should also say Ameen, because whoever's Ameen coincides with the Ameen of the angels, his previous sins will be forgiven."""
"449","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When any one of you says Ameen and the angels in the heavens say (Ameen), and these two coincide with each other, then his previous sins are forgiven."""
"450","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) that he reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the state of bowing (ruku‘), so before joining the row, he performed ruku‘. He mentioned this to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""May Allah increase your eagerness (for good deeds), but do not do this again."""
"451","‘Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) says that he performed prayer with the Commander of the Faithful, Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), in Basra, so the Commander of the Faithful, Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), reminded us of the prayer which we used to perform with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then (Sayyiduna Imran, may Allah be pleased with him) said that when he would stand up and when he would bow down, he would say the takbir (that is, Allahu Akbar)."
"452","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for prayer, he would say the takbeer when he stood up, then when he bowed for ruku he would say the takbeer, then when he raised his back from ruku he would say ""Sami' Allahu liman hamidah,"" then while still standing he would say ""Rabbana lakal hamd."""
"453","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) that his son Mus’ab prayed beside him. (Mus’ab) says: I joined both my palms together and then pressed them between my knees, so my father forbade me and said: We used to do this, but we were forbidden from it and were commanded to place our hands (in bowing) on our knees."
"454","Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the bowing (ruku‘) of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his prostration (sajdah), his sitting between the two prostrations, and (the state) when he would raise his head from bowing, were all nearly equal in duration, except for the standing (qiyam) and sitting (qu‘ud), which were longer."
"455","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his bowing and his prostrations: ((Subhanak Allahumma Rabbana wa bihamdika Allahumma ighfir li.)) ""O Allah! I declare Your purity. O our Lord! I praise You. O Allah! Forgive me."""
"456","It is narrated in another hadith from Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): ""In accordance with (the command of) the Qur'an."""
"457","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the Imam says 'Sami' Allahu liman hamidah', you should say 'Allahumma Rabbana lakal hamd.' Whoever's saying coincides with the saying of the angels (i.e., is in unison), all his past sins will be forgiven."""
"458","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` Indeed, I will bring the prayer of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) closer (that is, just as the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lead the prayer, I will also lead the prayer in the same way, because indeed my prayer is like the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)). And Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), after saying ""Sami' Allahu liman hamidah"" in the last rak'ah of Zuhr, 'Isha, and Fajr prayers, would recite the (supplication of) Qunoot, supplicating for the Muslims and cursing the disbelievers."
"459","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that during the time of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), Qunoot supplication was recited in Fajr and Maghrib (prayers)."
"460","Sayyiduna Rifa’ah bin Rafi’ Zurqi (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we were once praying behind the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), so (we saw that) when he (peace be upon him) raised his head from bowing, he said: “Sami’ Allahu liman hamidah.” Then a man behind him said: “Rabbana wa lakal hamdu hamdan kathiran tayyiban mubarakan fihi.” When the Prophet (peace be upon him) finished, he said: “Who was the one who spoke?” That man said: “It was I.” So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “I saw more than thirty angels racing to see which of them would write it down first.”"
"461","When `Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him)` used to describe the manner of the Prophet’s (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayer, he would demonstrate by performing the prayer. So when he would raise his head from bowing (ruku‘), he would stand up straight until we would say that surely he has forgotten (to go into prostration)."
"462","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would raise his head (from bowing), he would say: ""Sami' Allahu liman hamidah, Rabbana wa lakal hamd."" He would mention some people by name and supplicate for them, and he would say: ""O Allah! Rescue Walid bin Walid, Salama bin Hisham, 'Ayyash bin Abi Rabi'ah, and the weak Muslims (from the oppression of the disbelievers of Makkah). O Allah! Intensify Your punishment upon (the tribe of) Mudar, and afflict them with famine like the famine during the time of Yusuf (peace be upon him)."" At that time, the people of Mudar from the east were opposing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"463","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): Once, people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Do you have any doubt in seeing the moon on the night of the full moon when there are no clouds over it?"" The people replied, ""O Messenger of Allah! No."" He said, ""Do you have any doubt in seeing the sun when there are no clouds over it?"" They replied, ""No."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""So you will see your Lord in the same way. On the Day of Resurrection, people will be resurrected, then Allah, the Exalted, will say: 'Whoever used to worship something (in the world), let him follow it.' So some of them will follow the sun, some will follow the moon, and some will follow idols, and this group (of believers) will remain, and among them will also be the hypocrites of this Ummah. Then Allah, the Exalted, will come to them in a form which they do not recognize and will say, 'I am your Lord.' They will say, (We do not recognize You), we will remain here until our Lord comes to us, and when He comes, we will recognize Him. Then Allah, the Exalted, will come to them in a form which they recognize and will say, 'I am your Lord.' They will say, 'Yes, You are our Lord.' Then Allah will call them, and a bridge will be placed over the back of Hell. All the Prophets will cross it with their nations, and I will be the first among them to cross. On that Day, no one will speak except the Prophets, and the words of the Prophets on that Day will be: 'O Allah, grant safety, grant safety.' In Hell, there will be hooks like the thorns of Sa'dan. Have you seen the thorns of Sa'dan?"" The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) replied, ""Yes."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""They will be like the thorns of Sa'dan, except that no one knows their greatness except Allah. Those hooks will snatch people according to their deeds. Some will be destroyed (falling into Hell) due to their deeds, and some will be torn to pieces (by the wounds), then will be saved. Until, when Allah wills to show mercy to those among the people of Hell, He will command the angels to bring out those who used to worship Allah. So the angels will bring them out, and the angels will recognize them by the marks of prostration, and Allah has forbidden the Fire to consume the marks of prostration. So the Fire will consume the whole body of the son of Adam except the marks of prostration. They will be brought out from the Fire (in such a state that) they will be blackened, then the water of life will be poured over them, and (by its effect) they will grow as a seed grows in the flow of a stream. After that, Allah will finish judging between the servants, and one man will remain between Paradise and Hell, and he will be the last of the people of Hell to enter Paradise. His face will be towards Hell, and he will say, 'O my Lord! Turn my face away from Hell, for its air has poisoned me and its blaze has burnt me.' Allah will say, 'Well, if I do this favor for you, will you ask for anything else?' He will say, 'By Your Majesty, I will not ask for anything else.' Then Allah, the Exalted, will take from him as strong a promise as He wills, and Allah will turn his face away from Hell. When he turns towards Paradise and sees its freshness, he will remain silent as long as Allah wills, then he will say, 'O my Lord! Place me at the gate of Paradise.' Allah will say, 'Did you not make a promise that you would not ask for anything else besides what has already been given to you?' He will say, 'O my Lord! Do not make me the most miserable of Your creation.' Allah will say, 'If I grant you this, will you ask for anything else?' He will say, 'By Your Majesty, no, I will not ask for anything else.' Then Allah will take from him as strong a promise as He wills. So Allah will place him at the gate of Paradise. When he reaches the gate of Paradise and sees its freshness and joy, he will remain silent as long as Allah wills, then he will say, 'O my Lord! Admit me into Paradise.' Then Allah, the Exalted, will say, 'O son of Adam! How treacherous you are! Did you not make a promise that you would not ask for anything else besides what has already been given to you?' He will say, 'O my Lord! Do not make me the most miserable of Your creation.' Then Allah will laugh and be pleased with him. After that, He will permit him to enter Paradise and will say, 'Wish (i.e., ask for whatever you want).' So he will begin to wish until his wishes are exhausted. Then Allah, the Great and Glorious, will say, 'Ask for more.' Now Allah will remind him until, when all his wishes are finished, Allah will say, 'You are given all this (according to your wishes) and as much again.' (Upon hearing this hadith) Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said at this point: 'Allah, the Exalted, said: You are given all this and ten times as much.' So Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) replied, 'I remember from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) only this statement in the hadith: You are given all this and as much again.' So Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) said, 'I myself heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: You are given all this and ten times as much.'"""
"464","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones (these seven parts are): the forehead (along with the tip of the nose)."" While saying this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) pointed towards his nose. ""And both hands, both knees, and the toes of both feet, and it has also been commanded that we should not gather up our clothes or hair."""
"465","´Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I will not fall short in leading you in prayer just as I saw the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lead it.... This hadith has already passed (see the chapter: When one raises his head from bowing, he should stand calmly)."
"466","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Be moderate in prostrations, and none of you should spread his forearms (on the ground) like a dog spreads them."""
"467","Sayyiduna Malik bin Huwairith (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that he saw the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing prayer, and (he saw that) when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in an odd-numbered rak‘ah of his prayer, he would not stand up until he had sat straight."
"468","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that he led the prayer, and whenever he raised his head (first) from prostration and performed the second prostration, and when he raised his head (from the second prostration), and when he stood up after completing two rak'ahs, on all these occasions he said the takbeer aloud and said: I have seen the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing the same."
"469","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when (his father Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both) would sit in prayer, he would sit cross-legged. I also sat in the same way. I was young in those days, so (my father) Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) forbade me and said that the correct way of prayer is that you should raise your right foot and fold your left. Upon this, I said, ""You (i.e., Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both) also do the same."" He replied, ""My feet (have become weak and) cannot bear my weight."""
"470","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Humayd As-Sa’idi (may Allah be pleased with him): I remember the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) better than any of you. I saw that when he said the takbir (of opening), he raised both his hands up to the level of his shoulders. And when he bowed for ruku’, he placed both his hands firmly on his knees, then bent his back. And when he raised his head (from ruku’), he stood up straight until every bone returned to its place. And when he prostrated, he placed both his hands on the ground, neither spreading them out nor gathering them in, and he turned the toes of his feet towards the qiblah. Then, when he sat after two rak’ahs, he sat on his left foot and kept his right foot upright. Then, when he sat in the last rak’ah, he brought his left foot forward and kept his right foot upright and sat on his buttocks."
"471","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Buhaina (may Allah be pleased with him) says that he was from the tribe of Azd Shanu’ah and an ally of Banu Abd Manaf, and among the companions of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led the people in the Zuhr prayer (one day), and (by mistake) stood up after the first two rak’ahs and did not sit, so the people also stood up with him. When he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) completed the prayer and the people were waiting for him to say salam, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said takbeer while sitting and performed two prostrations before saying salam, and then he said salam."
"472","Narrated Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): When we used to pray behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in the sitting (tashahhud), we used to say: Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon Jibreel, peace be upon Mika'il, and peace be upon so-and-so and so-and-so. Then (once) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked towards us and said: ""Allah Himself is As-Salam (the Source of Peace), so what is the need to send peace upon Him? So when any of you prays, let him say: 'All verbal, physical, and financial acts of worship are for Allah. O Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! Peace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon all the righteous slaves of Allah.' For when you say this, this supplication will reach every righteous slave of Allah, whether he is in the heavens or on the earth. (And) I bear witness that there is no true deity except Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah."""
"473","‘Mother of the Believers, Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her),’ the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to make this supplication in prayer: “O Allah! I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the tribulation of the Dajjal, and I seek refuge in You from the trials of life and death. O Allah! I seek refuge in You from sin and debt.” Someone said that you seek refuge from debt very often (what is the reason for this?), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When a person becomes indebted, when he speaks, he lies, and when he makes a promise, he breaks it.”"
"474","It is narrated from Amir al-Mu'minin Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) that he requested the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), ""Teach me a supplication which I may recite in my prayer."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Recite this supplication: 'O Allah! I have greatly wronged myself and there is none to forgive sins except You, so forgive me with Your mercy and have mercy on me. Surely, You are the Most Forgiving, Most Merciful.'"""
"475","The hadith about the tashahhud of 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) has just been mentioned (see the chapter: One should also recite the tashahhud in the second sitting). Here in this narration, at the end of the hadith, it is stated that after this, whatever supplication he finds good and wishes to ask for, he may ask for it."
"476","Umm al-Mu'mineen Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) says that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) finished the prayer and said the salam, as soon as he had completed his salam, the women would stand up (and leave), and he (peace and blessings be upon him) would remain seated for a short while before standing up himself (that is, he would stay seated there). Imam Zuhri says: I think—and full knowledge is with Allah Almighty—that he (peace and blessings be upon him) would remain seated only so that the women could leave and the men, after finishing the prayer, would not encounter them."
"477","‘Sayyiduna Itban bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that’ we prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he (peace be upon him) said the salam (to end the prayer), we also said the salam."
"478","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that when the people finished the obligatory prayer, raising the voice in remembrance (of Allah) was (practiced) in the era of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) also said that when I used to hear the people returning while remembering (Allah), I would know that the prayer had been completed."
"479","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that some poor people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""The wealthy have obtained high ranks and everlasting bliss. They pray as we pray, and they fast as we fast (in other words, they participate in the acts of worship that we do), and they have more wealth, with which they perform Hajj, ‘Umrah, strive in jihad, and give charity."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you something, that if you act upon it, you will catch up with those who have surpassed you, and no one after you will overtake you, and you will be the best among those with whom you are, except for one who does the same as you? So after every prayer, recite Subhan Allah thirty-three times, Alhamdulillah thirty-three times, and Allahu Akbar thirty-three times."" The narrator says that after this, we differed among ourselves, and some of us said that we should recite Tasbih thirty-three times, Tahmid thirty-three times, and Takbir thirty-four times. So I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) again, and he said: ""Subhan Allah, Alhamdulillah, and Allahu Akbar — all should be recited thirty-three times each."""
"480","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Mughirah bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite (this supplication) after every obligatory prayer: “There is no deity except Allah, He is One, He has no partner, His is the dominion and for Him is all praise, and He is powerful over everything. O Allah! There is none who can withhold what You give, and none who can give what You withhold, and the effort of the striving person is of no benefit before You.”"
"481","Narrated Sayyiduna Samurah bin Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him): Whenever the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished a prayer, he would turn his blessed face towards us."
"482","Sayyiduna Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led the morning prayer at Hudaybiyyah after a night in which it had rained. When he finished the prayer, he turned to the people and said: ""Do you know what your Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, has said?"" They replied, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He has said: 'Some of My servants have become believers in Me, and some have become disbelievers.' Those who said, 'We have been given rain by the grace and mercy of Allah,' such people have believed in Me (i.e., Allah) and disbelieved in the stars (and the like). And those who said, 'We have been given rain because of such-and-such a star,' they have disbelieved in Me (i.e., Allah the Exalted) and believed in the stars."""
"483","Narrated Uqbah bin Al-Harith (may Allah be pleased with him): I offered the Asr prayer behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah. He (peace be upon him) finished the prayer with salam and stood up quickly, stepping over the necks of the people, and went to one of his wives’ rooms. The people were startled by his haste. When he (peace be upon him) returned and saw their astonishment at his speed, he (peace be upon him) said: “I remembered some gold that was with us, and I disliked that it should distract me from the remembrance of Allah, so I ordered it to be distributed.”"
"484","Narrated Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): None of you should give a share to Satan from his prayer by thinking that it is necessary for him (after the prayer) to turn only to his right side. Indeed, I have often seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turning to his left side."
"485","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats from this plant, i.e., garlic, should not come near our mosque and should not meet us."" The narrator (Ata) says: I asked, ""Which type of garlic is meant?"" Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: ""I only know that it refers to raw garlic or the smell of garlic."""
"486","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats garlic or onion should keep away from us,"" or he said, ""should keep away from our mosque and stay at home."" And once, a pot containing some cooked vegetables was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he perceived an odor in it. He asked, ""What is in it?"" All the vegetables in it were mentioned to him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Bring it closer to some of my companions who are with me."" When he saw that the companion also disliked eating those vegetables, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""You eat, for I converse with whom you do not converse."""
"487","In another narration, it is mentioned (Ibn Wahb says) that a ""badr""—that is, a tray or large plate—containing vegetables was brought to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him)."
"488","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a completely isolated (or orphaned child's) grave, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) led the people in prayer, and the people formed rows behind him, and he offered its (funeral) prayer."
"489","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Ghusl is obligatory upon every adult on the day of Jumu'ah (Friday)."""
"490","A person said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), ""Did you attend (the Eid prayer ground) with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)?"" He replied, ""Yes! If my close relationship with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had not existed, I would not have been able to attend (meaning due to my young age)."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to the place near the house of Kathir bin Salt, then he delivered the sermon. After that, he went to the women, advised them, reminded them of (Allah's commands), and instructed them to give charity. So, some women began to stretch their hands towards their rings, some towards their earrings, and some towards other jewelry, and they started taking them off and putting them in the sheet of Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) returned home."
"491","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""When your women ask your permission at night to go to the mosque (to perform prayer), then grant them permission."""
